# Binary files of the module go through Git LFS: git keeps a pointer of a few
# lines, the file itself lies beside it in the LFS store. Without this the history
# swells - git holds a whole copy of a binary on every change and shows no diff.
#
# The cost, stated because it decides what belongs here: LFS does NOT compress one
# version against another. Every edit is stored whole. So this list holds what a
# recipe cannot express and what changes rarely - not the output of every build.
#
# The plugins are the reason the list exists. They are small today, and a pointer
# for a 275-byte plugin costs about as much as the plugin - but the rule is about
# the kind of file, not its present size: a plugin grows with every record, and a
# rule applied only once it hurts is a rule nobody applies.
#
# The text source of a plugin is NOT here on purpose: esp/source/ is the Spriggit
# decomposition, it is text, and it has to diff and merge like any other source.
*.esp   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.esm   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.esl   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.bsa   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.nif   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tri   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.hkx   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.dds   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.7z    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
